## THE DECISIONS OF THIS COMMIT (each Tuesday's default as coordinator; each a Question at the stamp; each a behaviour with a cell, a mutant or a named limit)
- **D1 (FOUND 1; STOP-CLASS Q1): every exception the blob maker throws is `CodecFailed`, a cancellation included.** Both catches lose their filter. The paths it covers, by a grep of the library's 9 `.cs` files for `_codec.` (MEASURED: 2 hits, `CsaStore.cs:286` `_codec.SearchPrefix` and `:303` `_codec.Blob`, the only two calls of the maker): every call of the maker. No inner exception is attached (as F08 already asserts: the maker's own message never reaches a text). The caller's OWN cancellation is untouched: it is raised by the Graph layer at a request (cell L04, unchanged). DERIVED, named: when the caller has cancelled AND the maker throws a cancellation of its own, the call ends `CodecFailed` (the maker runs before the request that would raise the caller's cancellation), a typed failure, never an untyped one.
- **D2 (FOUND 2; STOP-CLASS Q2, Tuesday's default REFUSE): one whole-answer check in `GetJsonAsync`, after the parse and before anything is read.** The paths it covers, by a grep of the 9 files for a JSON parse (`JsonDocument.Parse|JsonSerializer|Utf8JsonReader|JsonNode|JsonElement.Parse`, MEASURED: 1 hit, `CsaStore.cs:242`) and of its callers (MEASURED: `GetJsonAsync(` called at `CsaStore.cs:165` the set read, `:171` the definition read, `:196` the search, `:213` the user read): every answer the store reads. The PATCH's answer is never parsed (`CsaStore.cs:140` discards it: DERIVED). The walk covers objects inside arrays (the search's `value`), and its depth is the parser's (DERIVED: `JsonDocument` refuses a document deeper than its default limit, which `GetJsonAsync` already turns into `MalformedAnswer`; the limit itself UNMEASURED here).
- **D3 (Q3): the set's own repeated-name check is removed, its rule held by D2's check alone.** At BASE `CsaReading.cs:67` to `:73` refused a name twice INSIDE the set; D2 refuses it everywhere, so a second check is dead code whose mutant (`mDuplicateNameTaken`, lane A2's) would survive. F07's "a name twice" row stays and is now red under the three D2 mutants that reach it.
- **D4 (Q2's cost, named in this kit and the README's sentence): fail closed also on a part the store never reads.** A repeated name in another attribute set, in `@odata.count`, in an unread property of a user, fails the whole call (cells F13 "count twice" and "a name twice in another set"). For a search, the cost is every lookup whose answer holds that user (bounded by the prefix: one card's holders). Whether Graph ever sends a repeated name: UNMEASURED (the gate's words).
- **D5: the cells.** Five new `[Theory]` methods, 24 `[InlineData]` rows, after the last cell of each file; no existing cell, helper or assertion changes (numstat +153 -0 over the four test files). Every red is `Assert.IsType<CsaStoreException>` failing on what the call ended in (the escaped cancellation, or null when the call answered): an assertion, never a throw out of the cell or a hang (each call races the existing 10 s `Kit.Done` bound). `[Fact]`/`[Theory]`/`[InlineData` by the indented pattern: Theories 17 to 22, InlineData 69 to 93, Facts 19 unchanged; column-1 `^\[(Fact|Theory|InlineData)` 0 (MEASURED per file).
